    "teacher_markdown": "### **Teacher Tips**\r\n\r\n**Students may think dot notation and bracket notation do different things**\r\n\r\nStudents often assume that dot notation and bracket notation are different operations rather than two ways to access the same property. Encourage them to compare the results by asking: **\"If both lines update the same property, what changes on the page?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\ndessert.name = \"Ice Cream\";\r\n```\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\ndessert[\"name\"] = \"Ice Cream\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nHelp students see that both approaches update the same value in the object.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may confuse property names with string values**\r\n\r\nWhen using bracket notation, students sometimes forget that the property name must be written as a string. Ask: **\"What is the name of the property you want to update?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\ndessert[\"flavor\"] = \"Vanilla\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nCompare with:\r\n```javascript\r\ndessert.flavor = \"Vanilla\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students recognize that bracket notation uses quotation marks around the property name.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may focus on the object update and miss the render step**\r\n\r\nSome students will successfully update the object but not connect those changes to what appears on the page. Encourage them to trace the flow of data by asking: **\"Which function reads the object and updates the display?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\nconst render = () => {\r\n  nameSpan.textContent = dessert.name;\r\n  flavorSpan.textContent = dessert.flavor;\r\n  frozenSpan.textContent = dessert.isFrozen;\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nRemind students that updating the object changes the stored data, and `render()` updates what the user sees.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may not notice where dot notation is already being used**\r\n\r\nStudents often focus on the new bracket notation and overlook the existing dot notation throughout the code. Ask: **\"How many examples of dot notation can you find in the starter code?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\ndessert.name\r\ndessert.flavor\r\ndessert.isFrozen\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students recognize that they have already been working with dot notation throughout the lesson."
  },
